      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa): restore automatic smoke coverage across channels",
        "body": "Related: #101164\nRelated: #101184\nSupersedes: #101187\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where automatic QA Smoke CI selected one shared multi-channel profile, causing the suite resolver to reject the run before any channel scenario could execute.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe workflow now plans three deterministic channel-compatible shards from the current smoke profile: one Matrix shard and two execution-cost-balanced Telegram shards. All 89 eligible flow, script, and Playwright scenarios run exactly once. Each shard runs independently while one aggregate required status stays fail-closed. Slack and WhatsApp restart/resume scenarios require their live channel drivers because Crabline does not satisfy those inbound/auth contracts; the silence-sensitive Telegram baseline is isolated from concurrent transport traffic.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMaintainers regain reliable automatic Matrix and Telegram smoke coverage without weakening the shared profile's cross-channel taxonomy. Slack and WhatsApp restart/resume coverage remains in the live-driver lanes instead of failing the simulated automatic lane.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact CI on the original sharding patch proved Matrix and one Telegram shard, then exposed the repaired contracts: unsupported simulated Slack/WhatsApp restart paths and concurrent Telegram traffic contaminating a silence assertion: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28820059322\n- Focused planner, scenario-catalog, suite-launcher, and workflow-guard coverage: 71 tests passed; 89 mixed-kind scenarios are selected exactly once across three shards.\n- Final exact-head CI: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28831595268 — Matrix, Telegram 1/2, Telegram 2/2, fail-closed aggregate, Windows, native i18n, and test types all passed.\n- Final exact-head Blacksmith Testbox: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28831595306 — passed.\n- `actionlint .github/workflows/ci.yml`, `node scripts/check-workflows.mjs`, targeted `oxfmt --check`, and `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Fresh structured autoreview on the complete replacement diff: clean, no accepted or actionable findings.\n- This PR replaces #101164, which GitHub would not reopen after its source branch was force-updated. It targets current `main` after #101184 reverted the temporary single-channel workaround.\n",
